From 490e174a09b9c4284e9074ed94615b59e5f73730 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsha Nanda <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:11:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: resolve protected provenance against the base remote

canonicalUpstreamRef() picked the feature branch's tracking remote. In a
fork-style checkout that is the contributor-owned `origin`, so a protected
change merged from the fork's default branch satisfied the ancestry check
even though it was never published to the official repository.

Extract Forge's existing base-remote resolver (upstream preferred over
origin) out of lib/commands/ship.js into lib/base-remote.js and reuse it
from the pre-commit check, so both surfaces agree on what the base is.
ship.js re-exports the same functions, so there is one implementation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
